\ rill/rt.4 - Rill's runtime, stage 1a (Iteration 736): text values in an
\ arena, joining them, and the boot word of Rill's image. Loaded after
\ the Forth libraries the shell's image also loads (SHELL-LANGUAGE.md
\ Part 5); none of relfsh's own sources.
\
\ A text value is one cell: the address of a cell holding its length,
\ its bytes after it. Numbers are cells. The arena is one block, bumped
\ and never freed piecemeal: a script's values live until it ends.

VARIABLE R-TOP   VARIABLE R-END
VARIABLE R-ARENA0  VARIABLE R-GC-AT  VARIABLE G-STRESS   \ the arena's start; where the next collection is due (776)
134217728 CONSTANT R-ARENA-SIZE
: R-ARENA-INIT ( --- )   R-ARENA-SIZE ALLOCATE THROW  DUP R-ARENA0 !  DUP R-TOP !  DUP R-ARENA-SIZE + R-END !  16777216 + R-GC-AT ! ;   \ 128 MB of address space, touched only as used (755: 16 MB filled by the pilot)
: R-ALLOT ( n --- addr )
  7 + -8 AND  R-TOP @ SWAP OVER + DUP R-END @ U> IF TRUE ABORT" rill: the arena is full" THEN  R-TOP ! ;   \ the test a branch, its message only when full (768)
: R-TEXT ( c-addr u --- t )   DUP CELL+ R-ALLOT >R  DUP R@ !  R@ CELL+ SWAP MOVE  R> ;
: R-T@ ( t --- c-addr u )   DUP CELL+ SWAP @ ;
VARIABLE RB-T
: R-BYTES ( b1 .. bn n --- t )   \ a text from n bytes on the stack: literals with " or a line end
  DUP CELL+ R-ALLOT RB-T !  DUP RB-T @ !
  BEGIN DUP WHILE  1-  SWAP OVER RB-T @ CELL+ + C!  REPEAT DROP  RB-T @ ;
: R-NUM ( n --- t )   DUP ABS 0 <# #S ROT SIGN #> R-TEXT ;
VARIABLE RC-N   VARIABLE RC-T   VARIABLE RC-P
: R-CONCAT ( t1 .. tn n --- t )   \ n texts joined, the deepest first
  RC-N !  0  RC-N @ 0 ?DO  I 1+ PICK @ +  LOOP
  DUP CELL+ R-ALLOT TUCK ! RC-T !
  RC-T @ DUP @ + CELL+ RC-P !
  RC-N @ 0 ?DO  R-T@ DUP NEGATE RC-P +!  RC-P @ SWAP MOVE  LOOP
  RC-T @ ;
: R-T= ( t1 t2 --- f )   >R R-T@ R> R-T@ COMPARE 0= ;
: R-TYPE ( t --- )   R-T@ TYPE ;
: R-NL ( --- )   10 EMIT ;

\ ---- Lists and records (stage 2, Iteration 739) -------------------------
\ An item of a list or a field of a record is a box: two cells, its kind
\ and its value - the one place values of different kinds meet (Part 5).
\ A list is [count][capacity][items], the items a cell array of boxes; a
\ record the same with a key array beside it, each key a text. Both grow
\ by a new array twice the size, the old one left in the arena.
: /STRING ( c-addr u n --- c-addr' u' )   TUCK - >R + R> ;   \ not in the kernel
1 CONSTANT K-NUM   2 CONSTANT K-TEXT   3 CONSTANT K-BOOL   4 CONSTANT K-LIST   5 CONSTANT K-REC   6 CONSTANT K-DEC
DEFER R-DEC>TEXT-HOOK   \ R-ANY>TEXT needs it before the library defines it
VARIABLE RL   VARIABLE RJ-SEP
: R-BOX ( v kind --- box )   2 CELLS R-ALLOT >R  R@ !  R@ CELL+ !  R> ;   \ boxsmall tried and taken out (752)
: R-UNBOX ( box --- v kind )   DUP CELL+ @ SWAP @ ;
: R-KIND-ERR ( --- )   ." rill: a value of the wrong kind" R-NL  -4001 THROW ;
: R-ANY>NUM ( box --- n )   R-UNBOX DUP K-NUM = OVER K-BOOL = OR 0= IF R-KIND-ERR THEN DROP ;
\ [gene truth]
: R-ANY>BOOL ( box --- f )   \ an item as a condition (751): an empty text, list or record false
  R-UNBOX  DUP K-TEXT = OVER K-LIST = OR IF DROP @ 0<> EXIT THEN  K-REC = IF @ @ 0<> EXIT THEN  0<> ;
\ [/gene]
: R-ANY>TEXT ( box --- t )
  R-UNBOX  DUP K-TEXT = IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP K-DEC = IF DROP R-DEC>TEXT-HOOK EXIT THEN                \ 754: decimals, defined later
  DUP K-NUM = IF DROP R-NUM EXIT THEN
  K-BOOL = IF IF S" true" ELSE S" false" THEN R-TEXT EXIT THEN
  S" (list or record)" R-TEXT ;
: R-NEW-LIST ( --- l )   3 CELLS R-ALLOT  0 OVER !  G-LISTCAP OVER CELL+ !  G-LISTCAP CELLS R-ALLOT OVER 2 CELLS + ! ;   \ genes 749
: R-LEN ( l --- n )   @ ;
: R-ITEMS ( l --- a )   2 CELLS + @ ;
: R-GROW ( l --- )   \ room for one more item
  DUP @ OVER CELL+ @ < IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP CELL+ @ DUP G-GROWTH * 2/ SWAP 1+ MAX DUP CELLS R-ALLOT     ( l cap2 a2 )   \ capacity * growth / 2, at least one more
  >R OVER R-ITEMS R@ 3 PICK @ CELLS MOVE         \ the items copied
  OVER CELL+ !  R> SWAP 2 CELLS + ! ;
: R-PUSH ( box l --- )   DUP @ OVER CELL+ @ < 0= IF DUP R-GROW THEN  DUP >R  2 CELLS + @ R@ @ CELLS + !  1 R> +! ;   \ R-GROW only when full (775)
: R-INDEX ( l i --- l i' )   \ an index the unsigned test refused: from the end when negative and in the list,
  \ as Python's $l[-1] (771); past either end an error. Reached only where the plain read would fail.
  DUP 0< IF OVER @ OVER + DUP 0< 0= IF NIP EXIT THEN DROP THEN
  ." rill: index " . ." past a list of " @ . R-NL -4002 THROW ;
: R-AT ( l i --- box )   OVER @ OVER U> 0= IF R-INDEX THEN  CELLS SWAP 2 CELLS + @ + @ ;
: R-SET ( box l i --- )   OVER @ OVER U> 0= IF R-INDEX THEN  CELLS SWAP R-ITEMS + ! ;
: R-SHIFT ( l --- box )   \ the first item, out
  DUP @ 0= IF ." rill: shift of an empty list" R-NL -4002 THROW THEN
  DUP R-ITEMS @ >R  DUP R-ITEMS DUP CELL+ SWAP 2 PICK @ 1- CELLS MOVE  -1 SWAP +!  R> ;
: R-EXTEND ( l m --- )   DUP @ 0 ?DO  DUP I R-AT 2 PICK R-PUSH  LOOP 2DROP ;
: R-BOUND ( n len --- n' )   OVER 0< IF + 0 MAX ELSE MIN THEN ;   \ a slice's bound: negative from the end, within the list
: R-SLICE ( l a b --- l2 )   \ items a up to (not with) b - negative bounds from the end, as Python's (771)
  \ The new list in a variable, not on the return stack: inside DO, R@
  \ is the loop's index - R-JOIN, R-SLICE and R-RANGE faulted on it.
  R-NEW-LIST RL !  2 PICK @ R-BOUND >R  OVER @ R-BOUND R>
  2DUP < IF SWAP ?DO  DUP I R-AT RL @ R-PUSH  LOOP ELSE 2DROP THEN  DROP  RL @ ;
: R-BOX= ( box1 box2 --- f )
  R-UNBOX ROT R-UNBOX ROT OVER <> IF 2DROP DROP 0 EXIT THEN    ( v2 v1 kind )
  K-TEXT = IF R-T= ELSE = THEN ;
VARIABLE RK-A  VARIABLE RK-U   \ a key's bytes, while it is looked for (775)
: R-IN ( box l --- f )   \ x in a list - a text compared in place with the items that are texts (775)
  OVER @ K-TEXT = IF
    SWAP CELL+ @ DUP CELL+ RK-A ! @ RK-U !  DUP @ SWAP 2 CELLS + @ SWAP
    0 ?DO  DUP I CELLS + @ DUP @ K-TEXT = IF CELL+ @ DUP @ RK-U @ = IF CELL+ RK-U @ RK-A @ RK-U @ COMPARE 0= IF
      DROP -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN ELSE DROP THEN ELSE DROP THEN  LOOP  DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  0 SWAP DUP @ 0 ?DO  DUP I R-AT 3 PICK R-BOX= IF NIP -1 SWAP LEAVE THEN  LOOP DROP NIP ;
\ records
VARIABLE RK
: R-NEW-RECORD ( --- r )   \ keys, values, and a hash table and its size (0 0: none yet; gene rechash, 750)
  4 CELLS R-ALLOT  R-NEW-LIST OVER !  R-NEW-LIST OVER CELL+ !  0 OVER 2 CELLS + !  0 OVER 3 CELLS + ! ;
: R-KEYS ( r --- l )   @ ;
: R-VALS ( r --- l )   CELL+ @ ;
\ [gene rechash]
: R-HASH ( t --- h )   R-T@ OVER + SWAP 2166136261 ROT ROT ?DO I C@ XOR 16777619 * LOOP ;   \ FNV-1a: its low 32 bits the same, no mask per byte (775)
: RH-TABLE ( r --- a )   2 CELLS + @ ;
: RH-CAP ( r --- n )   3 CELLS + @ ;
VARIABLE RH-R  VARIABLE RH-K
: RH-PROBE ( key r --- slot )   \ the slot holding the key's index + 1, or the empty one it would take
  RH-R ! RH-K !  RH-K @ DUP CELL+ RK-A ! @ RK-U !  RH-K @ R-HASH RH-R @ RH-CAP 1- AND
  BEGIN
    DUP CELLS RH-R @ RH-TABLE + DUP @
    DUP 0= IF DROP NIP EXIT THEN
    1- CELLS RH-R @ @ 2 CELLS + @ + @ CELL+ @                     \ the key at that index, its text (775: in place)
    DUP @ RK-U @ = IF CELL+ RK-U @ RK-A @ RK-U @ COMPARE 0= IF NIP EXIT THEN ELSE DROP THEN
    DROP 1+ RH-R @ RH-CAP 1- AND
  AGAIN ;
: RH-POW2 ( n --- p )   1 BEGIN 2DUP > WHILE 2* REPEAT NIP ;
: RH-BUILD ( r cap --- )   \ a table of cap slots for every key r has
  OVER 3 CELLS + !  DUP RH-CAP CELLS R-ALLOT DUP 2 PICK RH-CAP CELLS ERASE OVER 2 CELLS + !
  DUP @ R-LEN 0 ?DO  DUP @ I R-AT R-UNBOX DROP OVER RH-PROBE  I 1+ SWAP !  LOOP DROP ;
: RH-MAINTAIN ( r --- )   \ a key was added: past G-RECHASH keys a table, kept at most half full
  G-RECHASH 0= IF DROP EXIT THEN
  DUP @ R-LEN                                                  ( r n )
  OVER RH-TABLE 0= IF  DUP G-RECHASH > IF 4 * RH-POW2 RH-BUILD ELSE 2DROP THEN EXIT  THEN
  DUP 2* 2 PICK RH-CAP > IF 4 * RH-POW2 RH-BUILD EXIT THEN
  1- >R  DUP @ R@ R-AT R-UNBOX DROP OVER RH-PROBE  R> 1+ SWAP !  DROP ;
\ [/gene]
\ [gene rechash]
: R-FIND-LINEAR ( key r --- i | -1 )   \ key a text
\ [/gene]
\ [gene !rechash]
: R-FIND ( key r --- i | -1 )   \ key a text
\ [/gene]
  SWAP DUP CELL+ RK-A ! @ RK-U !  R-KEYS DUP @ SWAP 2 CELLS + @ SWAP      \ 775: each key's bytes compared in place
  0 ?DO  DUP I CELLS + @ CELL+ @  DUP @ RK-U @ = IF CELL+ RK-U @ RK-A @ RK-U @ COMPARE 0= IF DROP I UNLOOP EXIT THEN ELSE DROP THEN  LOOP
  DROP -1 ;
\ [gene rechash]
: R-FIND ( key r --- i | -1 )   \ through the table when the record has one
  DUP RH-TABLE IF RH-PROBE @ 1- EXIT THEN  R-FIND-LINEAR ;
\ [/gene]
: R-PUT ( box key r --- )
  2DUP R-FIND DUP 0< IF  DROP  >R K-TEXT R-BOX R@ R-KEYS R-PUSH  R@ R-VALS R-PUSH  R>
\ [gene rechash]
    RH-MAINTAIN
\ [/gene]
\ [gene !rechash]
    DROP
\ [/gene]
    EXIT  THEN
  ROT DROP SWAP R-VALS SWAP R-SET ;
: R-GET ( key r --- box )
  2DUP R-FIND DUP 0< IF DROP DROP ." rill: no field " R-TYPE R-NL -4003 THROW THEN  ROT DROP SWAP R-VALS SWAP R-AT ;
: R-HAS ( key r --- f )   R-FIND 0< 0= ;
\ texts and lists
VARIABLE SW-END
: R-SPLIT-WS ( t --- l )   \ the words of a text: runs of bytes above 32 (775: an address walked to an end, no /STRING a byte)
  R-NEW-LIST >R  R-T@ OVER + SW-END !
  BEGIN
    BEGIN DUP SW-END @ < IF DUP C@ 33 < ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1+ REPEAT
    DUP SW-END @ <
  WHILE
    DUP BEGIN DUP SW-END @ < IF DUP C@ 32 > ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1+ REPEAT
    TUCK OVER - R-TEXT K-TEXT R-BOX R@ R-PUSH
  REPEAT DROP R> ;
: R-LINES ( t --- l )   \ its lines; a last empty one not counted
  R-NEW-LIST >R  R-T@
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    2DUP 10 SCAN  2SWAP DROP                       ( a2 u2 a )   \ a2: at the LF, or the end
    2 PICK OVER - R-TEXT K-TEXT R-BOX R@ R-PUSH
    DUP IF 1 /STRING THEN
  REPEAT 2DROP R> ;
: R-JOIN ( l sep --- t )   \ the items as texts, sep between
  RJ-SEP !  0 SWAP  DUP @ 0 ?DO
    I IF RJ-SEP @ ROT 1+ ROT THEN  DUP I R-AT R-ANY>TEXT  ROT 1+ ROT
  LOOP DROP R-CONCAT ;
: R-RANGE ( a b --- l )   \ range(a, b): a up to, not with, b - Python's (770); empty when b <= a
  R-NEW-LIST RL !  OVER MAX SWAP ?DO  I K-NUM R-BOX RL @ R-PUSH  LOOP  RL @ ;
VARIABLE RG-S  VARIABLE RG-B
: R-RANGE-STEP ( a b step --- l )   \ range(a, b, step), as Python's: up while below b, or down while above it
  DUP 0= ABORT" rill: range's step is 0"
  RG-S ! RG-B !  R-NEW-LIST RL !
  BEGIN DUP RG-S @ 0> IF RG-B @ < ELSE RG-B @ > THEN WHILE  DUP K-NUM R-BOX RL @ R-PUSH  RG-S @ +  REPEAT
  DROP RL @ ;
: R-NUMBER ( t --- n )   R-T@ 0 0 2SWAP  OVER C@ [CHAR] - = DUP >R IF 1 /STRING THEN  >NUMBER NIP IF ." rill: not a number" R-NL -4004 THROW THEN DROP R> IF NEGATE THEN ;


\ Commands, pipelines, output captured, ports redirected (stage 1b,
\ Iteration 738). Rill's own executor on the kernel's FORK, EXECVE,
\ WAITPID, PIPE and DUP2 - nothing of the shell's. A program is found on
\ PATH by env, one exec more, until the search is written in Forth.
: R-CSTR ( t --- c-addr )   R-T@ DUP 1+ R-ALLOT >R  TUCK R@ SWAP MOVE  R@ + 0 SWAP C!  R> ;
VARIABLE RV-N   VARIABLE RV-V
: R-ARGV ( t1 .. tn n --- argv )   \ a NUL-ended vector in the arena, "env" first
  DUP RV-N !  2 + CELLS R-ALLOT RV-V !
  0  RV-V @ RV-N @ 1+ CELLS + !
  RV-N @ 0 ?DO  R-CSTR  RV-V @ RV-N @ I - CELLS + !  LOOP
  S" env" R-TEXT R-CSTR RV-V @ !  RV-V @ ;
: R-EXECV ( argv --- )   S" /usr/bin/env" R-TEXT R-CSTR EXECVE DROP  127 SYS-EXIT ;
: R-DECODE ( raw --- status )   DUP 127 AND IF 127 AND 128 + ELSE 8 RSHIFT 255 AND THEN ;

\ Redirections of the stage about to start: a file onto a descriptor
\ (text, mode, fd), or one descriptor onto another (-1, from, fd); the
\ child applies them in the order they were written.
8 CONSTANT RR-MAX
RR-MAX CELLS BUFFER: RR-T   RR-MAX CELLS BUFFER: RR-M   RR-MAX CELLS BUFFER: RR-F
VARIABLE RR-N
: R-RD-RESET ( --- )   0 RR-N ! ;
: R-RD-FILE ( t mode fd --- )
  RR-F RR-N @ CELLS + !  RR-M RR-N @ CELLS + !  RR-T RR-N @ CELLS + !  1 RR-N +! ;
: R-RD-DUP ( from fd --- )   >R -1 SWAP R> R-RD-FILE ;
: R-RD-APPLY ( --- )
  RR-N @ 0 ?DO
    RR-T I CELLS + @ -1 = IF  RR-M I CELLS + @  RR-F I CELLS + @  DUP2 DROP
    ELSE
      RR-T I CELLS + @ R-T@  RR-M I CELLS + @  OPEN-FILE IF
        DROP ." rill: cannot open " RR-T I CELLS + @ R-TYPE R-NL  1 SYS-EXIT
      THEN
      DUP RR-F I CELLS + @ DUP2 DROP  CLOSE-FILE DROP
    THEN
  LOOP ;

\ A pipeline: PL-BEGIN, a PL-STAGE a command (the last with a true
\ flag), PL-END. Every pipe end is listed, and each child closes them
\ all once its own are on 0 and 1 - or a reader would never see the end.
16 CONSTANT PL-MAX
PL-MAX CELLS BUFFER: PL-PIDS   VARIABLE PL-NP
PL-MAX 2* 2 + CELLS BUFFER: PL-FDS   VARIABLE PL-NF
VARIABLE PL-PREV  VARIABLE PL-CAPW  VARIABLE PL-CAPR
VARIABLE PL-IN  VARIABLE PL-OUT  VARIABLE PL-NEXT  VARIABLE PL-OWN
: PL-FD+ ( fd --- )   PL-FDS PL-NF @ CELLS + !  1 PL-NF +! ;
: PL-BEGIN ( capture? --- )
  0 PL-NP !  0 PL-NF !  -1 PL-PREV !  -1 PL-CAPW !  -1 PL-CAPR !  R-RD-RESET
  IF  PIPE THROW  DUP PL-CAPW ! PL-FD+  DUP PL-CAPR ! PL-FD+  THEN ;
: PL-CHILD ( in out --- )
  DUP -1 <> IF 1 DUP2 DROP ELSE DROP THEN
  DUP -1 <> IF 0 DUP2 DROP ELSE DROP THEN
  PL-NF @ 0 ?DO  PL-FDS I CELLS + @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  LOOP
  R-RD-APPLY ;
: R-ARGV-L ( l --- argv )   \ a list's items, as texts, a NUL-ended vector, "env" first (a spread, 744)
  DUP R-LEN DUP RV-N !  2 + CELLS R-ALLOT RV-V !
  0  RV-V @ RV-N @ 1+ CELLS + !
  RV-N @ 0 ?DO  DUP I R-AT R-ANY>TEXT R-CSTR  RV-V @ I 1+ CELLS + !  LOOP DROP
  S" env" R-TEXT R-CSTR RV-V @ !  RV-V @ ;
: PL-STAGE-V ( argv last? --- )
  >R  PL-PREV @ PL-IN !  -1 PL-NEXT !  0 PL-OWN !
  R> IF  PL-CAPW @ PL-OUT !
  ELSE  PIPE THROW  DUP PL-FD+ PL-OUT !  DUP PL-FD+ PL-NEXT !  -1 PL-OWN !  THEN
  FORK DUP 0= IF  DROP  PL-IN @ PL-OUT @ PL-CHILD  R-EXECV  THEN
  PL-PIDS PL-NP @ CELLS + !  1 PL-NP +!  DROP
  PL-IN @ -1 <> IF  PL-IN @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  THEN
  PL-OWN @ IF  PL-OUT @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  THEN
  PL-NEXT @ PL-PREV !  R-RD-RESET ;
: PL-STAGE ( t1 .. tn n last? --- )   >R R-ARGV R> PL-STAGE-V ;
: PL-STAGE-L ( argl last? --- )   >R R-ARGV-L R> PL-STAGE-V ;
: R-READ-KEEP ( fd --- t )   \ to its end, one text, as it is (read(), 754)
  >R  R-TOP @ ALIGNED DUP R-TOP !  DUP CELL+                 ( t p )
  BEGIN
    DUP 65536 + R-END @ U> ABORT" rill: the arena is full"
    DUP 65536 R@ READ-SOME DUP 0>
  WHILE + REPEAT  DROP R> DROP  OVER CELL+ -  OVER !  DUP @ CELL+ ALIGNED OVER + R-TOP ! ;
: R-READ-ALL ( fd --- t )   \ to its end, one text; one trailing newline off
  >R  R-TOP @ ALIGNED DUP R-TOP !  DUP CELL+                 ( t p )
  BEGIN
    DUP 65536 + R-END @ U> ABORT" rill: the arena is full"
    DUP 65536 R@ READ-SOME DUP 0>
  WHILE + REPEAT  DROP R> DROP                                ( t end )
  OVER CELL+ -                                                ( t len )
  DUP IF  OVER CELL+ OVER + 1- C@ 10 = IF 1- THEN  THEN
  OVER !  DUP @ CELL+ ALIGNED OVER + R-TOP ! ;
: PL-END ( --- [t] status )   \ t when captured; the status is the last stage's
  PL-CAPR @ -1 <> IF
    PL-CAPW @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  PL-CAPR @ R-READ-ALL  PL-CAPR @ CLOSE-FILE DROP
  THEN
  0  PL-NP @ 0 ?DO  DROP  PL-PIDS I CELLS + @ WAITPID DROP R-DECODE  LOOP ;
: R-EXEC ( t1 .. tn n --- status )   0 PL-BEGIN  -1 PL-STAGE  PL-END ;
VARIABLE R-STATUS
\ Ending, and what the script is given (Iteration 744)
CREATE R-NLB 10 C,
: R-ERR-TYPE ( t --- )   R-T@ 2 WRITE DROP  R-NLB 1 2 WRITE DROP ;   \ to the err port, a line
: R-FAIL ( t --- )   R-ERR-TYPE  1 R-STATUS !  -4000 THROW ;        \ fail "message": status 1
: R-EXIT ( n --- )   R-STATUS !  -4000 THROW ;                        \ exit n
VARIABLE R-ON-EXIT-XT
: R-ON-EXIT ( xt --- )   R-ON-EXIT-XT ! ;                             \ on EXIT { }: run when the script ends
: R-RUN-EXIT ( --- )   R-ON-EXIT-XT @ ?DUP IF 0 R-ON-EXIT-XT ! CATCH DROP THEN ;
: R-ARG ( n --- t )   \ arg(n): the script's nth argument, or empty
  DUP 0< OVER SYS-ARGC < 0= OR IF DROP 0 0 R-TEXT EXIT THEN  SYS-ARG DUP CSTRLEN R-TEXT ;
: R-SCRIPT ( --- t )   0 R-ARG ;
: R-ARGS ( --- l )   R-NEW-LIST  SYS-ARGC 1 ?DO  I R-ARG K-TEXT R-BOX OVER R-PUSH  LOOP ;
: R-ENV ( t --- t )   R-CSTR GETENV ?DUP IF DUP CSTRLEN R-TEXT ELSE 0 0 R-TEXT THEN ;
: R-DEFAULT ( t1 t2 --- t )   OVER @ IF DROP ELSE NIP THEN ;     \ the first unless it is empty
: R-CHECK ( status --- )   \ failure stops the script, with the status
  ?DUP IF  R-STATUS !  -4000 THROW  THEN ;

VARIABLE PX-XT
: PX-RUN ( --- )   \ in the child: the def, its failure its status (745)
  0 R-ON-EXIT-XT !  PX-XT @ CATCH ?DUP IF -4000 = IF R-STATUS @ ELSE 2 THEN SYS-EXIT THEN  0 SYS-EXIT ;
: PL-STAGE-X ( xt last? --- )   \ a def as a stage: run in a child, as a program would be
  >R  PL-PREV @ PL-IN !  -1 PL-NEXT !  0 PL-OWN !
  R> IF  PL-CAPW @ PL-OUT !
  ELSE  PIPE THROW  DUP PL-FD+ PL-OUT !  DUP PL-FD+ PL-NEXT !  -1 PL-OWN !  THEN
  FORK DUP 0= IF  DROP  PX-XT !  PL-IN @ PL-OUT @ PL-CHILD  PX-RUN  THEN
  PL-PIDS PL-NP @ CELLS + !  1 PL-NP +!  DROP
  PL-IN @ -1 <> IF  PL-IN @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  THEN
  PL-OWN @ IF  PL-OUT @ CLOSE-FILE DROP  THEN
  PL-NEXT @ PL-PREV !  R-RD-RESET ;
\ par for: each body in a child of its own, all waited for at the end (745)
VARIABLE R-BRK   \ break, from a loop body made a def of its own by a continue
64 CONSTANT PAR-MAX   PAR-MAX CELLS BUFFER: PAR-PIDS   VARIABLE PAR-N
: R-PAR-BEGIN ( --- )   0 PAR-N ! ;
: R-PAR-FORK ( --- child? )
  FORK DUP 0= IF DROP 0 R-ON-EXIT-XT ! -1 EXIT THEN             \ the child: not the script's on EXIT
  PAR-N @ PAR-MAX = ABORT" rill: par for has more than 64 bodies running"
  PAR-PIDS PAR-N @ CELLS + !  1 PAR-N +!  0 ;
: R-PAR-DONE ( --- )   0 SYS-EXIT ;
: R-PAR-END ( --- )   \ every body waited for; the first failure's status, if one failed
  0  PAR-N @ 0 ?DO  PAR-PIDS I CELLS + @ WAITPID DROP R-DECODE  OVER 0= IF NIP ELSE DROP THEN  LOOP
  R-CHECK ;

\ The image boots into R-BOOT: its first argument is the Forth that
\ tools/rillc.py made of a Rill script, evaluated; the image leaves with
\ status 0.
: R-SLURP ( c-addr u --- addr len )   \ a whole file, into the heap
  R/O OPEN-FILE ABORT" rill: cannot open the program" >R
  R@ FILE-SIZE THROW DROP  DUP ALLOCATE THROW      ( len buf )
  DUP ROT R@ READ-FILE THROW                        ( buf len' )
  R> CLOSE-FILE DROP ;
: R-BLANKS ( addr len --- addr len )   \ every control character a blank
  2DUP 0 ?DO  DUP I + C@ 32 < IF  32 OVER I + C!  THEN  LOOP DROP ;
DEFER R-COMPILE ( c-addr u --- c-addr2 u2 )   \ a .rill's text to Forth: rill/compile.4 sets it
: R-RILL? ( c-addr u --- f )   DUP 5 < IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN  + 5 - 5 S" .rill" COMPARE 0= ;
: R-RUN ( --- )
  \ Not INCLUDED: the boot word runs before the interpreter has a file
  \ to read from, and INCLUDED says "Error reading file" there; the
  \ program is read whole, its line ends made blanks, and EVALUATEd.
  SYS-ARGC 1 < ABORT" rill: usage: relf64 kernel64-rill.img PROGRAM.4"
  0 SYS-ARG DUP CSTRLEN 2DUP R-RILL? >R R-SLURP R> IF R-COMPILE THEN R-BLANKS EVALUATE ;
: R-INIT ( --- )
  \ What WARM and QUIT set before the interpreter reads - a boot word runs
  \ ahead of both, with the search order the build left (its wordlists'
  \ addresses from before the save), so EVALUATE there faulted.
  0 HANDLER !  DECIMAL  2 #ORDER !
  FORTH-WORDLIST CONTEXT !  FORTH-WORDLIST CONTEXT CELL+ !  FORTH-WORDLIST CURRENT !
  0 STATE !  TIB SRC !  0 SID !  INCLUDE-BUFFER INCLUDE-POINTER ! ;
\ ALLOC-BUFFERS first, as the shell's MAIN does: every BUFFER: (pool.4)
\ points into the heap of the session that built the image, gone at
\ the next run - shadow.4's LDECL-ADDRS among them, which is why a def
\ with locals, compiled after the load, wrote through a stale pointer
\ and faulted (Iteration 737). An error leaves with status 2.
\ R-RUN's xt kept as an offset (!XT): ['] in a definition compiles the
\ absolute address, which the save and reload leave pointing at nothing -
\ the CATCH that faulted at boot (Iteration 737), and why shell.4's
\ DO-FORTH keeps its EVALUATE the same way.
VARIABLE R-RUN-XT   ' R-RUN R-RUN-XT !XT
: R-BOOT ( --- )
  ALLOC-BUFFERS  R-INIT  R-ARENA-INIT
  S" RILL_GC_STRESS" R-TEXT R-ENV @ IF -1 G-STRESS !  0 R-GC-AT ! THEN     \ a collection at every safe point: the tests' (776)
  0 R-ON-EXIT-XT !
  R-RUN-XT @XT CATCH ?DUP IF
    R-RUN-EXIT                                        \ on EXIT runs however the script ends
    DUP -4000 = IF  DROP R-STATUS @ SYS-EXIT  THEN    \ a command failed, fail, exit: its status
    ." rill: error " . R-NL  2 SYS-EXIT
  THEN  R-RUN-EXIT  0 SYS-EXIT ;

\ ---- The library for the Python-born scripts (Iteration 754) ----------------
\ Texts, files, records sorted and sliced, and decimals: fixed point, six
\ places (733's decision), a number scaled by a million - a library over */,
\ the engine unchanged.
: R-READ ( path --- t )   \ read(path): the file's whole text
  DUP R-T@ R/O OPEN-FILE IF DROP ." rill: cannot read " R-TYPE R-NL -4006 THROW THEN
  NIP DUP >R R-READ-KEEP R> CLOSE-FILE DROP ;
: R-WRITE ( path t --- )   \ write(path, text): the file made, or made again, holding the text
  SWAP DUP R-T@ W/O OPEN-FILE IF DROP ." rill: cannot write " R-TYPE R-NL -4006 THROW THEN
  NIP SWAP R-T@ 2 PICK WRITE-FILE DROP CLOSE-FILE DROP ;
: R-STARTS ( t prefix --- f )   \ < takes tu: three cells left, not four - a text shorter than the prefix
  \ dropped a cell too many, and the pilot's 2,402 lines ran the stack under (755)
  R-T@ ROT R-T@ ( pa pu ta tu ) 2 PICK < IF 2DROP DROP 0 EXIT THEN  OVER COMPARE 0= ;
: R-ENDS ( t suffix --- f )
  R-T@ ROT R-T@ 2 PICK OVER > IF 2DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN    ( sa su ta tu )
  2 PICK - + OVER COMPARE 0= ;
VARIABLE RC-LO  VARIABLE RC-HI  VARIABLE RC-D
: R-CASE ( t lo hi delta --- t2 )   \ a copy, each byte from lo to hi moved by delta
  RC-D ! RC-HI ! RC-LO !  R-T@ R-TEXT
  DUP R-T@ 0 ?DO  DUP I + C@ DUP RC-LO @ RC-HI @ 1+ WITHIN IF RC-D @ + OVER I + C! ELSE DROP THEN  LOOP DROP ;
: R-UPPER ( t --- t2 )   [CHAR] a [CHAR] z -32 R-CASE ;
: R-LOWER ( t --- t2 )   [CHAR] A [CHAR] Z 32 R-CASE ;
: R-TRIM ( t --- t2 )   \ blanks, tabs and line ends off both ends
  R-T@  BEGIN DUP IF OVER C@ 33 < ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1 /STRING REPEAT
  BEGIN DUP IF 2DUP + 1- C@ 33 < ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1- REPEAT  R-TEXT ;
: R-CLAMP ( n len --- n' )   OVER 0< IF + 0 MAX ELSE MIN THEN ;     \ negative from the end, as Python's
: R-TSLICE ( t a b --- t2 )   \ slice(text, a, b): characters a up to (not with) b
  >R >R R-T@ R> R>  2 PICK R-CLAMP  SWAP 2 PICK R-CLAMP SWAP  2DUP > IF DROP DUP THEN
  >R >R DROP R> R>  OVER - >R + R>  R-TEXT ;
VARIABLE RS-NEW
: R-RSLICE ( r a b --- r2 )   \ slice(record, a, b): its entries a up to (not with) b
  R-NEW-RECORD RS-NEW !  2 PICK R-KEYS R-LEN R-CLAMP >R  OVER R-KEYS R-LEN R-CLAMP R>
  2DUP < IF SWAP ?DO  DUP R-VALS I R-AT  OVER R-KEYS I R-AT R-ANY>TEXT  RS-NEW @ R-PUT  LOOP ELSE 2DROP THEN  DROP  RS-NEW @ ;
: R-AT-OR ( r key default --- box )   \ at(record, key, default): the field, or the default
  >R SWAP 2DUP R-HAS IF R> DROP R-GET ELSE 2DROP R> THEN ;
: R-SUM ( l --- n )   0 SWAP DUP R-LEN 0 ?DO DUP I R-AT R-ANY>NUM ROT + SWAP LOOP DROP ;
VARIABLE SB-R  VARIABLE SB-F  VARIABLE SB-DESC  VARIABLE SB-IX  VARIABLE SB-N
: SB-KEY ( i --- n )   SB-R @ R-VALS SWAP R-AT R-UNBOX DROP  SB-F @ SWAP R-GET R-ANY>NUM ;
: SB-BEFORE? ( i j --- f )   SWAP SB-KEY SWAP SB-KEY  SB-DESC @ IF > ELSE < THEN ;
: SB@ ( k --- i )   CELLS SB-IX @ + @ ;
: SB! ( i k --- )   CELLS SB-IX @ + ! ;
: R-SORT-BY ( r field order --- r2 )   \ sort-by(record, field, asc|desc): its entries by their values' field, stable
  S" desc" R-TEXT R-T= SB-DESC !  SB-F !  DUP SB-R !  R-KEYS R-LEN SB-N !
  SB-N @ CELLS R-ALLOT SB-IX !  SB-N @ 0 ?DO I I SB! LOOP
  SB-N @ 1 MAX 1 ?DO                                        \ 1 MAX: 0 1 ?DO would run the unsigned range
    I SB@  I
    BEGIN DUP 0> IF OVER OVER 1- SB@ SB-BEFORE? ELSE 0 THEN WHILE  DUP 1- SB@ OVER SB!  1- REPEAT
    SB!
  LOOP
  R-NEW-RECORD  SB-N @ 0 ?DO  SB-R @ R-VALS I SB@ R-AT  SB-R @ R-KEYS I SB@ R-AT R-ANY>TEXT  2 PICK R-PUT  LOOP ;
: R-BASE ( t --- t2 )   \ base(path): what follows its last /
  R-T@ DUP  BEGIN DUP IF 2 PICK OVER + 1- C@ [CHAR] / <> ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1- REPEAT  /STRING R-TEXT ;
40 BUFFER: DT-BUF   VARIABLE DT#
: DT+ ( c-addr u --- )   DT-BUF DT# @ + SWAP DUP DT# +! MOVE ;
: R-DEC>TEXT ( d --- t )   \ a decimal as text: its digits, trailing zeros after the point dropped, one kept
  0 DT# !  DUP 0< IF S" -" DT+ THEN  ABS 1000000 /MOD
  0 <# #S #> DT+  S" ." DT+
  0 <# # # # # # # #>  BEGIN DUP 1 > IF 2DUP + 1- C@ [CHAR] 0 = ELSE 0 THEN WHILE 1- REPEAT  DT+
  DT-BUF DT# @ R-TEXT ;
