\ ---- What the second pilot needs (Iteration 758) ---------------------------
: R-CMP ( b1 b2 --- n )   \ Python's order: numbers by value, texts by bytes, lists item by item, then length
  OVER @ OVER @ 2DUP <> IF > IF 2DROP 1 ELSE 2DROP -1 THEN EXIT THEN DROP
  DUP K-TEXT = IF DROP CELL+ @ R-T@ ROT CELL+ @ R-T@ 2SWAP COMPARE EXIT THEN
  K-LIST = IF  CELL+ @ SWAP CELL+ @ SWAP
    OVER R-LEN OVER R-LEN MIN 0 ?DO
      OVER I R-AT OVER I R-AT RECURSE ?DUP IF NIP NIP UNLOOP EXIT THEN
    LOOP
    R-LEN SWAP R-LEN SWAP 2DUP = IF 2DROP 0 ELSE < IF -1 ELSE 1 THEN THEN EXIT THEN
  CELL+ @ SWAP CELL+ @ SWAP 2DUP = IF 2DROP 0 ELSE < IF -1 ELSE 1 THEN THEN ;
VARIABLE SRT
: R-SORT ( l --- l2 )   \ sort(list): a copy, in Python's order, stable
  R-NEW-LIST SRT !  DUP R-LEN 0 ?DO DUP I R-AT SRT @ R-PUSH LOOP DROP
  SRT @ R-LEN 1 MAX 1 ?DO
    SRT @ I R-AT  I
    BEGIN DUP 0> IF OVER SRT @ 2 PICK 1- R-AT R-CMP 0< ELSE 0 THEN WHILE
      SRT @ OVER 1- R-AT SRT @ 2 PICK R-SET 1-
    REPEAT  SRT @ SWAP R-SET
  LOOP SRT @ ;
VARIABLE SP-L  VARIABLE SP-A  VARIABLE SP-U
: SP-FIND ( a u --- i | -1 )   \ where the separator first stands: SCAN to its first byte, COMPARE there (775)
  OVER >R
